WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.134 --> 00:00:19.454
As soon as I finished my muffin, I went across the hall to Molly's apartment.

2
00:00:19.455 --> 00:00:25.555
Molly came to the door wearing her purple bathrobe and eating a chocolate-covered donut.

3
00:00:25.556 --> 00:00:30.242
"I'm having a mental health day," Molly announced.

4
00:00:30.243 --> 00:00:33.754
Tate had told me all about mental health days.

5
00:00:33.755 --> 00:00:41.743
You get to sit around in your pajamas, watching TV and eating your favorite foods.

6
00:00:41.744 --> 00:00:46.694
"Well, I'm having an emergency!" I said.

7
00:00:46.695 --> 00:00:49.532
Molly stopped chewing her donut.

8
00:00:49.533 --> 00:00:54.489
"What's wrong?" she asked. "Is somebody sick?"

9
00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:56.021
I shook my head.

10
00:00:56.022 --> 00:00:58.614
"No one is sick—except me.

11
00:00:58.615 --> 00:01:02.872
I'm sick of my cousin, Oliver, and he isn't even here yet!"

12
00:01:02.873 --> 00:01:05.089
Molly looked puzzled.

13
00:01:05.090 --> 00:01:07.150
"Iggy," she said.

14
00:01:07.151 --> 00:01:09.712
"What are you talking about?"

15
00:01:09.713 --> 00:01:14.379
"I'm talking about my bratty cousin, Oliver," I said.

16
00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:19.936
"He's coming to visit, and he's going to share my room!"

17
00:01:19.937 --> 00:01:24.547
I told Molly about Oliver visiting over winter vacation.

18
00:01:24.548 --> 00:01:30.936
"My mom said Aunt Julia and Uncle John want to take a cruise," I added.

19
00:01:30.937 --> 00:01:34.217
"Without Oliver?" asked Molly.

20
00:01:34.218 --> 00:01:38.854
I nodded. "My uncle has been working really hard.

21
00:01:38.855 --> 00:01:42.023
They want to take a vacation by themselves."

22
00:01:42.024 --> 00:01:49.954
Molly giggled. "They probably want to get away from Oliver for a while!"

23
00:01:49.955 --> 00:01:53.751
"I bet you're right," I said glumly.

24
00:01:53.752 --> 00:01:57.236
"But why do they have to leave him with us?"

25
00:01:57.237 --> 00:02:02.934
Just then we heard Josh and Jenny walking up the stairs with their dad.

26
00:02:02.935 --> 00:02:05.744
Molly and I looked down.

27
00:02:05.745 --> 00:02:08.722
They were all carrying grocery bags.

28
00:02:08.723 --> 00:02:12.044
"I've got a problem!" I burst out.

29
00:02:12.045 --> 00:02:13.783
Josh looked up at me.

30
00:02:13.784 --> 00:02:16.109
"Really?" he said.

31
00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:19.442
"Maybe we'd better have a powwow."

32
00:02:19.443 --> 00:02:25.062
My friends and I have a "powwow" whenever somebody has a big problem.

33
00:02:25.063 --> 00:02:28.028
We get together to figure out a solution.

34
00:02:28.029 --> 00:02:31.063
"That's a great idea!" I said.

35
00:02:31.064 --> 00:02:34.030
"I'll go get dressed," said Molly.

36
00:02:34.031 --> 00:02:38.278
"A powwow sounds like more fun than a mental health day."

37
00:02:38.279 --> 00:02:44.096
"We'll meet in five minutes outside on the front steps!" said Josh.

38
00:02:44.097 --> 00:02:47.345
Soon we were all sitting on the front steps.

39
00:02:47.346 --> 00:02:52.125
But it was freezing outside, and an icy rain had started to fall.

40
00:02:52.126 --> 00:02:57.286
"Let's go inside by the radiator," said Jenny.

41
00:02:57.287 --> 00:03:02.249
We went into the front hall and stood by the big radiator.

42
00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:05.930
It was making loud banging noises.

43
00:03:05.931 --> 00:03:09.337
But at least the front hall was warm.

44
00:03:09.338 --> 00:03:13.447
I told Josh and Jenny about Oliver's coming to visit.

45
00:03:13.448 --> 00:03:17.266
"And he's going to share my room!" I groaned.

46
00:03:17.267 --> 00:03:21.420
"So I won't have any quiet time to work on a new invention.

47
00:03:21.421 --> 00:03:26.212
And I really wanted to get into the Inventor's Hall of Fame!"

48
00:03:26.213 --> 00:03:29.597
"How do you do that?" asked Josh.

49
00:03:29.598 --> 00:03:33.862
"You have to invent something really amazing," I explained.

50
00:03:33.863 --> 00:03:37.563
"And if you do invent something cool, you win a trophy.

51
00:03:37.564 --> 00:03:43.082
Plus, you get your picture on the Inventor's Hall of Fame website."

52
00:03:43.083 --> 00:03:45.054
Molly's face lit up.

53
00:03:45.055 --> 00:03:48.083
"You would be famous, Iggy!"

54
00:03:48.084 --> 00:03:51.983
"But now Oliver is coming," I said.

55
00:03:51.984 --> 00:03:55.018
"He'll spoil everything!"

56
00:03:55.019 --> 00:03:58.437
"It could be fun," said Josh.

57
00:03:58.438 --> 00:04:00.902
He was trying to cheer me up.

58
00:04:00.903 --> 00:04:03.615
"You'll be like a big brother to Oliver."

59
00:04:03.616 --> 00:04:07.783
"Me, a big brother?" I said.

60
00:04:07.784 --> 00:04:10.752
I had to admit I hadn't thought of that.

61
00:04:10.753 --> 00:04:16.164
"We could fix him a cute little bed in your room," Jenny chimed in.

62
00:04:16.165 --> 00:04:21.080
"And invent games and fun activities to do!" added Molly.

63
00:04:21.081 --> 00:04:27.188
I smiled. "You guys are the best friends ever!" I said.

64
00:04:27.189 --> 00:04:30.002
I was starting to feel a little better.

65
00:04:30.003 --> 00:04:34.385
Maybe Oliver's visit wouldn't be so bad after all.

66
00:04:34.386 --> 00:04:38.860
I'm glad I didn't have a crystal ball to see the future right then.

67
00:04:38.861 --> 00:04:43.127
Because if I'd had a crystal ball, I would have seen the truth.

68
00:04:43.128 --> 00:04:52.293
Oliver was going to be trouble—big trouble!
